course: dictionary
lesson: 13891
title: Hard work and long tasks
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Laborious means needing a lot of hard work, effort and time. Building a castle stone by stone was laborious, because many workers had to lift heavy stones for a long time.
explain: Look at the words around it for clues. «Cleaning the whole house by hand was laborious.» The words by hand and the whole house tell you the job was long and tiring, so laborious means hard work.
explain: Laborious can also describe writing or speech. «His laborious speech was slow and heavy, with too much effort.» Here the word shows that the speaker worked too hard to get the words out, and it made the listeners bored.
explain: To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence. «The climb was laborious» still makes sense if you read it as «The climb was hard work and took a long time», so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Laborious means needing a lot of hard work, effort and time.
fact: «Counting one by one is laborious», so people in maths use multiplication to save time and effort.
fact: When writing or speech is laborious, it is slow and heavy, and it shows too much effort.
fact: Laborious comes from the Latin word labor, which means work.
fact: A laborious task is often long and tiring, like building a pyramid.
exercise: «Building the pyramids was a laborious task.» What does laborious mean here? | *Needing a lot of hard work and time | Very colourful and bright | Happy and full of fun | Quick and easy to finish
exercise: «Sorting ten thousand beads one by one was laborious.» Why might the author choose laborious? | Because the job took only one second | *Because the job was long and tiring | Because it was a party | Because the beads were shiny
exercise: Sam says laborious means lazy. Is he right? | Yes, it means happy and relaxed | Yes, it means lazy and doing nothing | *No, it means needing hard work, effort and time | No, it means very small
test: «Writing the whole report by hand was laborious, and his pen ran dry twice.» What does laborious suggest? | Coloured and bright | Needing no effort at all | Quick and cheerful | *Needing a lot of hard work and time
test: «His laborious reply was slow and heavy, with too much effort.» Which meaning fits laborious best? | *Slow and heavy, showing too much effort | Very fast and light | Short and kind | Loud and funny
exam: Which sentence uses laborious correctly? | «The laborious sun shone brightly over the beach.» | *«Digging the trench by hand was laborious, so the team took all day.» | «She laborious laughed at the joke.» | «The laborious puppy slept on the mat.»
